View the **execution process** of an intent (work), unlike get_worker_output which only gives the final conclusion. Three usages:
① Pass only intent_id → returns a stream of summaries for every step of that work (summary ≤100 chars, includes step_id; only an outline of actions, not the full output);
② intent_id + q → returns only the step summaries matching the keyword (searched in both summaries and full output; still only summaries, use ③ to see content);
③ intent_id + step_ids → returns the full content (detail) of those steps; at most 5 at a time, any extra returns only the first 5 and the ones not fetched are reported in notice/omitted_step_ids.
Typical flow: first use ①/② to locate the step_id of a suspicious step, then use ③ to fetch its full output. Thinking steps are not included. Historical traces of directly related tasks are supported; their results carry source_task_id/inherited=true and are read-only.
